# Officina Kreuzberg

> Officina Kreuzberg is a member-run coworking space in Berlin Kreuzberg, near Hermannplatz on the Kreuzberg–Neukölln border. There is no operator and no staff: the members rent the space together and share the work of running it, and joining means taking on a small share of that.

- Address: Jahnstraße 13, 10967 Berlin, Germany — ground floor, a few minutes' walk from Hermannplatz (U7, U8).
- Email: hello@officina.berlin
- Access: 24/7, weekends included. The door opens with an app on your phone, so there is no physical key to collect.
- Included with every desk: fast internet, a printer, coffee and tea, a big kitchen and a terrace — and a place in the collective: shared lunches, after-work drinks, and people to ask when you are stuck.
- Who works here: freelancers, remote employees and researchers — developers, designers, illustrators, architects, a data scientist, a policy coordinator, a copywriter, a filmmaker. Many of us work with NGOs and social projects.
- Languages: the site is in English at https://www.officina.berlin/en/ and in German at https://www.officina.berlin/de/.

